WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.740
Look at that! Yeah...
Did you know - candle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:09.900
flames conduct electricity better than air.
That is because there are ions in the flame,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:14.220
positively and negatively charged particles&nbsp;
resulting from the combustion process.&nbsp;

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:17.700
It's kind of a plasma.
And you can see that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:22.380
flame has two separate pieces two it now.
One is going towards the negative plate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.660
those would be the positive ions.&nbsp;
And the negative ions would be going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:28.320
toward the positively charged plate.
These two plates are charged up to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:32.220
20,000 volts, which in air can make a 2 cm spark.&nbsp;

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:37.080
But through the candle flame, it can make&nbsp;
a much larger spark because of those ions.&nbsp;

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:41.820
There are even ions in the smoke, which is why&nbsp;
it separates into two streams. The positive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:45.060
charges go to the negative plate and the&nbsp;
negative charges to the positive plate.

